  "contract": [
    "Initialize two100-byte channel groups at offsets0 and100, three125-element float records at200/216/232 and one125-element extended s16 record at248. Preserve reserved gaps.",
    "Each channel initializes capacities25, live window+12,25,1, signed125/window and signed125/period at0/16/32/48/64/84. Allocation receives full32-bit quotient/count; metadata fields truncate to16 bits.",
    "Short pair writes zero header, initializes125 s16 elements at+4, then reads the live divisor and truncates signed125/divisor to16 bits before passing it to the second s16 queue at+16.",
    "Extended queue allocates count*2 with32-bit wrapping only when buffer is null, then writes pointer/index/capacity/flags and low-byte mode in native order; returns0.",
    "A shared header corrects the caller declarations to the verified word-return API without changing its machine object. No duplicate native implementation or new state owner."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The670 direct comparisons execute all288 native instruction bytes and actual C float/base-s16 queue providers. Allocator is modeled; complete allocation words, public record images, provider snapshots and divisor read order compare, with independent mathematical allocation-sequence oracles.",
    "Only nonzero signed divisors are admitted. The existing descriptor builder unconditionally supplies5/25/25 for the known constructor path. Zero-divisor malformed descriptors and CCR divide-trap behavior are outside this API proof; no fallback behavior is asserted.",
    "Signed extreme nonzero divisors and full-width counts are symbolic allocation-boundary checks, not proof that large/negative allocations are physically valid. Null allocation models verify resulting metadata behavior; real allocator failure is nonreturning and remains governed by its separate receipt.",
    "The614-case constructor replay executes the actual new session/short-pair graph with only allocation, weights getter and model creation modeled. The128 real-C-heap lifecycle cases execute all recovered session and short-pair allocations, constructor and complete teardown; only weights/model resource ports remain modeled and model creation returns null. All recovered allocations coalesce back to the prior top.",
    "Prior same-ELF copy-probe evidence governs instrumentation: scoped owner observation and full memory comparisons avoid the broad Unicorn write-hook discrepancy. No new broad write trace is claimed. Active FP context is primed; exact FPSCR, saved integer/FP registers, SP, masks and guards compare. Cold activation, concurrency, invalid pointers, caller scratch/APSR/private frames are excluded.",
    "Source cannot execute stock; modeled ports return through BX LR. No executable opcode arrays or firmware traps are added to C.",
    "All870 other prior nongenerated source/object pairs remain unchanged, and the corrected caller machine object is also unchanged. Tested new/constructor objects equal the normal882-unit build; no new writable state or imports. Application imports fall66 to64; boot remains22.",
    "Weights getter and model construction, other algorithm constructors and hardware dependencies, final executable linking/startup, physical sensors and boot remain open. Relocatable composition is not bootable firmware; no instruction or image identity is claimed."
  ],
